# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Root-level ignore rules.
#
# SPA-Student-Portal/.gitignore only governs files inside that folder. Anything
# placed at the REPO ROOT is covered by this file instead, and without it a
# .env sitting next to the root server.js shim would be committed with the real
# admin password in it. That is the one mistake here that cannot be undone by
# deleting the file later — the secret stays in the git history.
#
# Real secrets belong in the host's Environment/Variables settings, never in a
# committed file. .env.example (inside the app folder) is the safe template.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local logs and OS clutter.
*.log
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Nothing installed or generated at the root is worth committing.
node_modules/
